Subject: [PATCH 0/4] Silicon Mitus SM5714 combo PMIC: fuel gauge and Type-C CC
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The Silicon Mitus SM5714 is a combo PMIC integrating a battery charger,
a fuel gauge and a Type-C/USB block. On the Samsung Galaxy A52 (SM7125)
each block is wired to a separate I2C address, and the Type-C block sits
on a different I2C bus from the charger and fuel gauge, so the blocks are
described as independent I2C devices rather than as MFD sub-nodes.

This series adds the two blocks that are self-contained and verified
working on the Galaxy A52:

  - the fuel gauge (battery voltage, current, temperature, capacity);
  - the Type-C CC detection block (attach/detach -> USB role switch plus
    VBUS in host role; no USB PD).

The charger block (charging control, OTG VBUS regulator, torch LED) is
not included yet; it needs more cleanup before it is ready.

No public datasheet is available; register layouts come from the Samsung
downstream driver and were verified on the device.

Patches 1-2 add the bindings, patches 3-4 the drivers.

Miroslav Mráz (4):
  dt-bindings: power: supply: add Silicon Mitus SM5714 fuel gauge
  dt-bindings: usb: add Silicon Mitus SM5714 Type-C CC detection
  power: supply: add Silicon Mitus SM5714 fuel gauge driver
  usb: typec: add Silicon Mitus SM5714 Type-C CC driver

